---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
---

<CaseStudy
  name="Trove"
  title="Trove 3D Printing"
  tagline="was an early stage consumer 3D printing startup backed by Resolute Ventures. Trove sought to bring consumer 3D printing to a new audience via fine jewelry customized in-browser."
  shareImage="project-thumb_trove"
  details={[{ label: 'Years', items: ['2014–2016'] }]}
>
  <Fragment slot="meta">
    <p class="callout">
      🔔 Trove was acquired by Classpass in 2016. It was a failure but also my first time designing anything so I'm still
      proud of it.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'customizer-mockup', alt: 'Trove customizer on desktop' }]} eager />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>
      I co-founded a consumer 3D-printing startup that created jewelry customized in-browser. I designed every part of
      the customer journey from site to packaging.
    </h2>
    <p>
      Trove was a customizable jewelry platform where users were able to discover, customize, and purchase their own
      unique jewelry pieces. The in-browser customization tools allowed anyone to create unique pieces without any
      experience with design programs.
    </p>
    <p>
      I co-founded Trove alongside Brian Park and Tim Growney in 2015. I designed everything that a user engaged with -
      brand, website, jewelry, packaging, and more. Being the only designer for the platform helped me to maintain a
      consistent user experience from initial awareness of Trove all the way to receiving and wearing our custom
      jewelry.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="gif">
    <img src="/media/customizer-mock-2-1.gif" alt="Animated demo of the Trove jewelry customizer" width="781" height="575" loading="lazy" />
  </figure>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'mobile-customizer@2X', alt: 'Trove customizer on mobile' }]} />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>I LEARNED A LOT.<br />THE HARD WAY.</h2>
    <p>
      As the first major product launch for a new founding team, the Customizer proved to be an invaluable learning
      experience. Internally, we learned how to effectively communicate with one another and discuss ideal products
      versus feasibility given short timelines. We began the ongoing process of deeply understanding our users and
      continue to refine this knowledge in order to continue to build better products.
    </p>
    <p>
      While it is drilled into UX designers to test, iterate, and refine, going through this process at a rapidly moving
      startup truly brought to light the urgency and importance of this process. Our success relies heavily on this
      design process and continual desire to explore and learn how we can innovate in ways that benefit our audience.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'BOXES2', alt: 'Trove jewelry packaging' }]} />
</CaseStudy>

<style>
  .gif {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(60px, 8vw, 100px);
  }
  .gif img {
    margin-inline: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
</style>
